# The terminal face's two files, relative to $HOME (~/.tsnake_highscore, ~/.tsnake_setup),
# which is also where they land if this checkout is ever someone's HOME. Player history, not
# source. The overlay's pair is not listed because it cannot appear here any more: the overlay
# names its engine's files under $XDG_STATE_HOME/tsnake, out of reach of the shell's plugin
# watcher — which is the price of a record that survives a reinstall. ./uninstall.sh is the
# command that erases them, deliberately; `omarchy plugin remove` cannot (no host hook, no
# manifest field), and that is the host's own convention rather than a leak.
